responses; CRITICAL GAP: _UPDATE_ISSUE_MUTATION (gh_client.py:65-73) does not select updatedAt in response shape; watermark capture requires mutation expansion or post-mutation fetch\\n5. Lifecycle divergence rules (5 cases) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: resolved by user 2026-06-04 \u2014 remote close\u2192resolve local, local resolve\u2192close GitHub, remote delete (not dirty)\u2192delete local, remote delete (dirty+content edit)\u2192re-create+relink, remote delete (dirty+closure)\u2192no-op\\n6. Per-section timestamp format (ISO 8601 UTC, parseable) | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker VERIFIED \u2014 entry_blocks.py timestamps are ISO 8601 UTC with Z terminator, parseable via datetime.fromisoformat()\\n7. Per-backend scope: beads=zero sync, GitHub=full model | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: item spec explicitly specifies backend-specific behavior; user confirmed 2026-06-04\\n8. Timeout primitives in gh_client.py | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: grep gh_client.py \u2014 get_github(timeout=15) at line 1159; Github(auth=..., timeout=timeout) at line 1181; try_get_github uses timeout=10 at line 1199\\n9. asyncio/locking primitives in server context | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: grep sync_state.py \u2014 SyncState.lock: asyncio.Lock at line 95; design constraint documented: lazy init inside running event loop; asyncio.to_thread in sync_engine.py:109\\n10. Serialization approach for concurrent writes | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: sync_state.py:95 \u2014 SyncState.lock: asyncio.Lock \\\"serialising sync workers\\\"; same primitive extends to foreground/background serialization\\n11. Outbox retry policy (cadence, driver, persistence format) | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: MISSING | Tried: grep for dirty/outbox/pending_push \u2014 zero matches; no existing outbox infrastructure. Options: (a) background reconcile loop re-pushes dirty items each cycle; (b) explicit retry command; (c) both. Design decision deferred to task decomposition \u2014 does not block planning\\n12. Cross-module API stability: sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py | (New) \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst \u2014 github_task.py calls _update_issue_graphql at lines 411, 446 and reads node[\\\"updatedAt\\\"] at line 166; directly inspectable; coordination required during implementation\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Conditions 1,2,4,5,6,7: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (fact-checker VERIFIED + user confirmation)\\n- Condition 3: AVAILABLE confirmed (fact-checker VERIFIED ungated background sync)\\n- Conditions 8,9,10: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (grep tool results: timeout=15 in get_github; asyncio.Lock in sync_state.py:95)\\n- Condition 12 (NEW): AVAILABLE \u2014 impact-analyst discovered sam_schema cross-module consumer\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 11\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 1\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\nRationale: All DERIVABLE conditions resolved via tool results. 1 MISSING (outbox retry policy) is a design choice resolvable during task decomposition \u2014 it does not represent unknown unknowns. Planner may proceed. Flag outbox retry policy as a pre-implementation design sub-decision in task T1 or the architecture spec.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code - Producers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py::BacklogItemMetadata` - New `pending_push` (dirty flag) field must be added to the model. Existing `last_synced` and `updated_at` fields are already present as watermark slots but the conditional-read path is not wired. Existing `BacklogItem` top-level shortcuts `last_synced` and `updated_at` (lines 903-904) also need review for consistency with new semantics. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Central data model; all serialization paths derive from it; all four backends receive it\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py::_write_issue_node_to_cache` - Current implementation overwrites local body+metadata from GitHub unconditionally. Must be replaced by watermark comparison + dirty-flag guard (no overwrite when item is locally dirty). | Risk: HIGH | Why: This is the background-sync conflict bug root: no timestamp comparison, no dirty check\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py::refresh_local_cache_from_github` - Full-fetch path (~66k token file). Must be split into watermark-incremental fetch (batch `{number, updatedAt}` query, then selective pull) + dirty-item protection. Backend-gating check must be added (no-op under non-GitHub backends). | Risk: HIGH | Why: Observed 10-minute hang source; produces silent data loss on every background startup\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py::sync_push_groomed_content` - Serial per-item `updateIssue` loop (~105 serial round-trips observed). Must become batched aliased mutations + bounded timeout per call. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Direct cause of the serial hang; no pacing, no timeout, no retry\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py::sync_items` - Caller that orchestrates sync_push_groomed_content and refresh_local_cache_from_github. Must adopt outbox/retry pattern and backend gating. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Top-level sync entry point; behavioral contract changes propagate to all callers\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py::merge_item_models` - Delegates to `get_config().backend.merge_item(local, remote)`. Must be verified that the consistent merge semantics (local metadata authoritative, section union, per-entry struck-wins/longer-wins) is the single path used everywhere \u2014 not bypassed by `_write_issue_node_to_cache`. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Three different merge behaviors exist currently; this redesign consolidates to one\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/gh_client.py::_UPDATE_ISSUE_MUTATION` - GraphQL mutation string. Requires `updatedAt` in the response selection set so the returned watermark can be stored after a successful push. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Without this field returned, watermark update-on-push is impossible; all write-through semantics depend on it\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/gh_client.py::_update_issue_graphql` - Function wrapping `_UPDATE_ISSUE_MUTATION`. If the redesign adds a required watermark param or changes return type to include `updatedAt`, callers in `sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py` break. If the function is extended internally only (mutation body expanded, return dict grows a key), existing callers stay compatible. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Cross-module consumer `github_task.py` calls this at lines 411 and 446; signature change escalates to HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/gh_client.py::sync_issues_graphql` - GraphQL fetch used by background sync. Must return `updatedAt` per issue to enable watermark comparison. Already returns `updatedAt` in `_parse_issue_node` / `IssueNode` (confirmed in `test_backlog_core_github.py` line 112) \u2014 verify the field flows through to the comparison site. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Fetch response shape is the foundation for watermark comparisons; missing field silently disables incremental sync\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github_sync.py::merge_item` - Currently wired only into the YAML pull path. Redesign requires this to be the single merge path for all sync directions (background cache write, push after remote-moved, conflict). | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Behavioral change: previously not called from `_write_issue_node_to_cache`; now it must be\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github_sync.py::render_issue_body` - Embeds a 4-field hardcoded allowlist in the `<!-- backlog-metadata: -->` block (`priority`, `type`, `status`, `added`). The new `pending_push`/`dirty` field does NOT appear in this block. No change required here \u2014 verified safe design. | Risk: LOW | Why: Allowlist is hardcoded, not a loop over all metadata fields; dirty flag cannot leak into GitHub body\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/sync_engine.py::_startup_sync_loop` - Launches background sync as an asyncio task. Must add backend-gating check: no-op (or `SyncStatus.OFFLINE` immediately) when the active backend is not `github`. Currently only kill-switch + re-entry guard exist. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Without gating, the loop hits GitHub API under sqlite/memory/beads backends; confirmed in item description\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/sync_state.py::SyncState` - Process-singleton holding sync status, retry count, timing. May need new fields for the outbox queue reference, dirty-item count, or watermark of last incremental pass. Must remain asyncio.Lock-safe. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Structural changes here flow into server.py startup, sync_engine, and all api_state tool responses\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/yaml_io.py::save_item` + `load_item` - Local YAML persistence layer for `BacklogItemMetadata`. New `pending_push` field must round-trip correctly through YAML serialization (save) and deserialization (load). | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: If the field is not declared with proper alias/serialization on the Pydantic model, YAML round-trip silently drops it\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py::BacklogBackend` - Protocol that all four backends implement. New capability flags or sync-specific methods (e.g., `supports_background_sync`) required for backend gating. Adding a non-optional method to a `@runtime_checkable` Protocol forces all implementations to implement it or fail Protocol conformance. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Any Protocol surface change breaks all four implementors simultaneously\\n\\n### Code - Consumers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py` - Primary BacklogBackend implementor. Implements `merge_item`, `sync_*` delegations, and the write-through path. Must implement new capability flags, bounded timeouts on all GitHub requests, and adopt the outbox/retry pattern. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Owns the complete sync surface; all behavioral changes land here first\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/beads_backend.py` - Must no-op any new sync-specific Protocol methods. Currently has no sync functionality; must not acquire any via default inheritance if a mixin is added. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Protocol fan-out; must remain deliberately inert for sync operations\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/sqlite_backend.py` - Local-only backend. Must no-op new sync Protocol methods. Explicit no-op guard also ensures `sync_engine` background loop exits cleanly without attempting GitHub API calls. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Protocol fan-out; sqlite is local-only by design\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/memory_backend.py` - In-memory test double. Must no-op new sync Protocol methods. Tests relying on memory backend's behavior must not accidentally trigger sync paths. | Risk: LOW | Why: Test double with no persistence; lowest consequence of any protocol change\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py::_backlog_lifespan` - Launches `_startup_sync_loop` in the lifespan context manager. Must add backend-identity check before `create_task`: if `create_backend()` returns a non-GitHub backend, do not launch the task. Currently only a kill-switch boolean and re-entry guard exist (lines 1560-1565). | Risk: HIGH | Why: Root of the \\\"sync runs under all backends\\\" defect confirmed in item description\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` - Exposes `backlog_sync`, `backlog_pull`, and `api_state` MCP tools. `api_state` reports `SyncState` fields; new outbox/watermark state fields will appear here. `backlog_pull` semantic changes (watermark-incremental vs full-fetch) visible to callers. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: MCP tool signatures and semantics change; callers through the plugin cache observe new behavior\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/close_test_issues.py` - Consumes `sync_issues_graphql` from `gh_client` to fetch open test issues by title/state. Does not process `updatedAt` \u2014 reads only title/state fields. Remains compatible if `sync_issues_graphql` response shape is extended (additive). | Risk: LOW | Why: Reads non-watermark fields only; compatible as long as field addition is non-breaking\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py` - **Cross-subsystem consumer.** Calls `_update_issue_graphql(repo, node[\\\"id\\\"], body=...)` at lines 411 and 446, and reads `node[\\\"updatedAt\\\"]` at line 166. If `_update_issue_graphql` gains a required watermark parameter, these calls break at runtime. If the mutation body expands internally with no signature change, they remain compatible. Must be verified against the final API design. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Cross-module boundary; SAM subsystem consumes a backlog_core transport function; conditional HIGH if signature changes\\n\\n### Code - Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/entry_blocks.py` - Provides per-section entry timestamps. Item description notes these as \\\"usable as fine-grained watermarks.\\\" No changes required in this redesign unless section-level watermarks are adopted (currently not in scope). | Risk: LOW | Why: Read-only reference; watermark design uses `updatedAt` (issue-level) not entry timestamps\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/rendering.py` - Backend-agnostic rendering shared by all three local backends. Provides `SECTION_HEADING` consumed by `github_sync.py`. No changes required unless section rendering changes as part of the metadata block update. | Risk: LOW | Why: Structural dependency not on the changed sync surface\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/_branch_delegates.py` - Thin wrapper routing branch operations through `BacklogBackend`. If new Protocol methods use the same delegation pattern, this file's structure is a reference for implementation. No direct changes required. | Risk: LOW | Why: Reads BacklogBackend but does not consume sync methods\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_github_sync.py` - Tests for `merge_item`, `render_issue_body`, `parse_issue_body`. If `merge_item` is now called from additional code paths, existing tests may need scenario expansion. Dirty-flag and watermark arguments to merge must be exercised. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Core merge semantics change; tests must cover all three previously-inconsistent paths now unified\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_github.py` - Tests `_parse_issue_node`, `_update_issue_graphql`, and related GraphQL response parsing. Importing `make_update_issue_response` from `graphql_factories`. Tests already verify `updatedAt` in fetch responses (line 112, 128) \u2014 but update response tests do not yet include `updatedAt`. Must be extended when `_UPDATE_ISSUE_MUTATION` is expanded. | Risk: HIGH | Why: `updatedAt` in update responses is the critical watermark source; untested path means watermark-on-push is unverified\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/graphql_factories.py::make_update_issue_response` - Returns `{id, number, state}` (line 269) \u2014 no `updatedAt`. When `_UPDATE_ISSUE_MUTATION` is expanded to return `updatedAt`, this factory must add the field or all tests using it test an obsolete response shape. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Factory is the mock backbone for all update-mutation tests; stale shape means tests pass against wrong response\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_sync_issues_graphql.py` - Tests `sync_issues_graphql`. Verifies current response shape. If the fetch query is modified to return additional watermark fields, mock shapes must be updated in lockstep. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Query expansion breaks response mock shapes\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_cross_backend.py` - Parametrized test suite covering InMemoryBackend and SQLiteBackend. **GitHubBackend tests are skipped by default** (require network access). The backend that implements the new sync surface is the one with no automated coverage in CI. New Protocol methods (capability flags, sync methods) on GitHub backend will not be exercised by this suite without explicit test additions or a mock-GitHub variant. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Protocol conformance gap \u2014 the primary implementor is CI-excluded; new surface is unverified at test time\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_startup_sync.py` - Tests the background sync loop. Must be extended to cover backend-gating: assert that the loop does not execute when backend is not `github` (memory/sqlite/beads). Currently the gating does not exist, so this test is missing. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Backend-gating is a new behavior with no test; without it the silent GitHub-API-under-wrong-backend defect persists\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_sync_scope.py` - Tests sync scope behavior. Must be reviewed for coverage of watermark-incremental path (batch `{number, updatedAt}` fetch + selective pull) vs full-refresh path. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: New sync modes need distinct test scenarios\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_concurrent_writes.py` - Tests concurrent write behavior. The outbox (asyncio.Queue) and asyncio.Lock serialization are directly in scope for this test file. Coverage of pending-push state under concurrent foreground writes + background reconcile must be added. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Outbox correctness and lock serialization are the core concurrency safety properties; no existing tests cover the new design\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` - Tests operations.py. `sync_items`, `sync_push_groomed_content`, `refresh_local_cache_from_github`, and `_write_issue_node_to_cache` are all in scope. Must verify bounded timeout behavior, dirty-flag protection, and watermark-comparison logic. | Risk: HIGH | Why: All redesigned operations live here; test suite must be extended substantially\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py` - Live integration test. May exercise the full sync path under real GitHub credentials. If live tests validate timing/hang behavior, they must be updated for the new batched/timeout-bounded flow. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Observed 10-minute hang was a live-environment issue; live tests are the correct validation gate for bounded-timeout correctness\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/conftest.py` - Shared fixtures for the tests/ directory. May need new fixtures for: mock SyncState with non-GitHub backend, mock asyncio.Queue outbox, and BacklogItemMetadata instances with the new `pending_push` field. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Fixture gaps propagate to all tests that need new state shapes\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` - **Required update per CLAUDE.md trigger.** Describes BacklogBackend Protocol methods (line 114) and the GitHub backend sync surface. Must be updated to document: new capability flags, `pending_push` field, watermark semantics, timeout bounds, outbox pattern, and backend-gating rule. The current description (`backlog_sync` via `sync_issues_graphql`, full-fetch) will be inaccurate after the redesign. | Risk: HIGH | Why: CLAUDE.md states \\\"When extending backend providers... read first. Amend that document\\\"\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` - Describes the end-to-end issue journey. The read/write/list/background-reconcile behavior described in this item's desired-behavior spec is a lifecycle change. Must be updated to reflect: offline-first write-through, dirty state, watermark-incremental reads, conflict resolution rule. | Risk: HIGH | Why: CLAUDE.md lists this as required reading for \\\"backlog lifecycle, grooming, or issue state machine\\\" changes; data structure change trigger applies\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/graphql-usage-guide.md` - Documents GraphQL query/mutation patterns in this codebase. Expanding `_UPDATE_ISSUE_MUTATION` to include `updatedAt` and adding the batch `{number, updatedAt}` fetch query are changes this guide must document. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: GraphQL patterns are the reference for future contributors; undocumented mutation expansions accumulate as implicit knowledge\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/DOCUMENTATION_DRIFT_AUDIT.md` - Drift audit log. If the audit was written against the current sync behavior, it becomes stale. | Risk: LOW | Why: Audit document, not behavioral spec; secondary update\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/SKILL.md` - Agent-facing skill describing `backlog_pull` and `backlog_sync` semantics. The description of `backlog_pull` as \\\"merges GitHub issue body content into local files, keeping the longer version\\\" (line 410) and `backlog_sync` description must be reviewed against new watermark-incremental behavior. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Agent instructions become misleading if they describe full-fetch semantics after incremental redesign\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/README.md` - User-facing README describing sync operations. \\\"GitHub Issues are the source of truth\\\" (line 412) and pull/sync behavior descriptions (lines 382-410) may need updating. | Risk: LOW | Why: Narrative accuracy; behavioral contract for agents comes from SKILL.md\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/CLI_TO_MCP_MIGRATION.md` - Migration guide mapping `backlog sync` \u2192 `backlog_sync` and `backlog pull` \u2192 `backlog_pull`. If the semantic behavior of these tools changes (watermark-incremental vs full-fetch), the migration guide's equivalence claims become misleading. | Risk: LOW | Why: Migration reference, not an agent instruction file; behavioral change is a secondary note\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/backlog-sync.yml` - Calls `backlog_sync` MCP tool via `fastmcp call`. Runs on push to `main` targeting `.claude/backlog/**` paths. The redesigned `backlog_sync` behavior (watermark-incremental, dirty/outbox, backend-gated) is the direct target of this workflow. If the tool's behavior changes to offline-first with pending-push semantics, the CI workflow still functions as the trigger for the outbox flush \u2014 but the operation sequence may produce different file-change outputs. Requires end-to-end validation after the redesign. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: CI workflow is the production trigger for the sync path being redesigned; behavioral change in backlog_sync propagates here\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py` - MCP server entry point. If new environment variables (timeout values, outbox queue size, backend-gating flag) are introduced, this script's startup configuration changes. No direct behavioral change unless the server argument interface changes. | Risk: LOW | Why: Entry point; affected only if new config params are required at startup\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/SKILL.md` - (Also listed in Documentation) This is an AI-facing agent instruction file. Instructions for `backlog_pull` state \\\"merges GitHub issue body content into local files keeping the longer version\\\" \u2014 this describes the existing merge-biased-toward-local behavior. Post-redesign the watermark-incremental read path changes when pulls occur and how conflicts are resolved. An AI reading stale instructions will invoke `backlog_pull` expecting full-merge semantics when the actual behavior is watermark-gated. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Prompt engineering artifact; behavioral mismatch leads to incorrect agent decisions about when to call pull vs relying on background sync\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finally.md` - Instructs agents: \\\"backlog_groom writes each section to GitHub synchronously as it runs \u2014 no explicit flush step is required.\\\" and \\\"Do NOT call `backlog_sync()` \u2014 that runs a full sweep of all issues and is expensive.\\\" The new write-through design changes the groom flush model \u2014 each groom write may now queue a pending-push rather than immediately writing through. The \\\"no flush required\\\" claim needs verification against the new design. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Agent instruction file; if groom no longer writes synchronously, agents following this instruction will silently leave items in dirty/pending state\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` | Role: producer | Connection: defines `BacklogItemMetadata` with `last_synced`, `updated_at` fields; new `pending_push` field required here | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'BacklogItemMetadata'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` | Role: producer | Connection: implements `_write_issue_node_to_cache`, `refresh_local_cache_from_github`, `sync_push_groomed_content`, `sync_items`, `merge_item_models` \u2014 all are being redesigned | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: '_write_issue_node_to_cache'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/gh_client.py` | Role: producer | Connection: owns `_UPDATE_ISSUE_MUTATION`, `_update_issue_graphql`, `sync_issues_graphql`; mutation needs `updatedAt` in response | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: '_UPDATE_ISSUE_MUTATION'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github_sync.py` | Role: producer | Connection: owns `merge_item` (becomes the single conflict model); `render_issue_body` verified safe (hardcoded 4-field allowlist) | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM | pattern: 'merge_item'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/sync_engine.py` | Role: producer | Connection: owns `_startup_sync_loop`; needs backend-gating before launching background task | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: '_startup_sync_loop'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/sync_state.py` | Role: producer | Connection: owns `SyncState` process singleton; may need outbox/watermark fields | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM | pattern: 'SyncState'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/yaml_io.py` | Role: producer | Connection: `save_item`/`load_item` must persist `pending_push` field through YAML round-trip | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM | pattern: 'save_item'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` | Role: producer | Connection: `BacklogBackend` Protocol; new capability flags or sync methods required for backend gating | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'BacklogBackend'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: primary implementor; receives all new Protocol methods + bounded timeout requirement | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/beads_backend.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: Protocol fan-out; must no-op new sync methods | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/sqlite_backend.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: Protocol fan-out; must no-op new sync methods | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/memory_backend.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: Protocol fan-out; must no-op new sync methods; low consequence | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: lifespan launches background sync without backend gating; `api_state` tool reports SyncState fields | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: '_backlog_lifespan'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: calls `_update_issue_graphql` and reads `updatedAt` from IssueNode \u2014 cross-module consumer of the changed transport function | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM | pattern: '_update_issue_graphql'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/close_test_issues.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: calls `sync_issues_graphql` but reads only title/state \u2014 not the watermark fields | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_github.py` | Role: test | Connection: tests `_parse_issue_node` and `_update_issue_graphql`; update-response tests lack `updatedAt` | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'make_update_issue_response'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/graphql_factories.py` | Role: test | Connection: `make_update_issue_response` returns `{id, number, state}` only \u2014 missing `updatedAt` for post-redesign mutation | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'make_update_issue_response'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_sync_issues_graphql.py` | Role: test | Connection: tests sync_issues_graphql response shape; query expansion changes mock shapes | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_github_sync.py` | Role: test | Connection: tests merge_item; must cover unified merge across all three previously-inconsistent paths | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM | pattern: 'merge_item'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_cross_backend.py` | Role: test | Connection: parametrized backend conformance suite; GitHubBackend excluded from CI by default; new Protocol surface unverified | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_startup_sync.py` | Role: test | Connection: tests background sync loop; backend-gating behavior not yet tested | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_sync_scope.py` | Role: test | Connection: tests sync scope; must cover watermark-incremental vs full-refresh paths | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_concurrent_writes.py` | Role: test | Connection: tests concurrent writes; outbox queue + asyncio.Lock serialization are new concurrency targets | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` | Role: test | Connection: tests operations.py sync functions; must cover bounded timeout, dirty-flag protection, watermark comparison | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'sync_push_groomed_content'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py` | Role: test | Connection: live integration test exercising real sync path; validates bounded-timeout correctness | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/conftest.py` | Role: test | Connection: shared fixtures; needs new fixtures for non-GitHub SyncState, asyncio.Queue outbox, BacklogItemMetadata with pending_push | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: authoritative Protocol reference; CLAUDE.md requires amendment on backend changes | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: lifecycle docs for read/write/background sync; all three behaviors change | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/graphql-usage-guide.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: documents mutation and query patterns; mutation expansion must be recorded | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/SKILL.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: describes backlog_pull/backlog_sync semantics for agents; full-fetch description becomes stale | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finally.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: instructs \\\"no explicit flush step required\\\"; may become inaccurate under pending-push model | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `.github/workflows/backlog-sync.yml` | Role: ci | Connection: triggers backlog_sync on push; behavioral change in sync propagates; requires end-to-end validation | Action: CI_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py` | Role: configuration | Connection: MCP server entry point; affected if new config params or env vars are required | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- Overall system risk: HIGH\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` - Protocol fan-out: adding any non-optional method breaks all four backends simultaneously; the primary GitHub implementor has no CI-gated conformance test\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py::_backlog_lifespan` - Background sync runs under all backends today; no backend-gating means GitHub API is called under sqlite/memory/beads\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests/graphql_factories.py::make_update_issue_response` + `test_backlog_core_github.py` - `updatedAt` missing from update-mutation test fixtures; watermark-on-push is the core correctness property and it has no test coverage\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_concurrent_writes.py` - Outbox/asyncio.Lock serialization has no existing tests for the new design\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py` - Cross-module consumer of `_update_issue_graphql`; risk escalates to HIGH if that function's signature changes\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - compatibility (Protocol fan-out to four backends)\\n  - verification (missing conformance coverage for GitHubBackend; missing update-mutation watermark tests)\\n  - behavioral (three inconsistent sync paths must collapse to one consistent merge model)\\n  - operational (background sync runs under wrong backends in production today)\\n  - scope (cross-subsystem consumer in